WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.360 --> 00:00:04.800
All good things must come to an end,&nbsp;
but some good things come to an end&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:04.800 --> 00:00:09.180
more than once. These TV shows ended up&nbsp;
on the chopping block multiple times.

00:00:09.960 --> 00:00:13.860
"Taxi" premiered on ABC all the way back in 1978,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:13.860 --> 00:00:18.720
featuring a cast of current and future&nbsp;
stars of the late '70s and early '80s as&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:18.720 --> 00:00:23.340
a collective of New York City taxi drivers.&nbsp;
The show starred the likes of Judd Hirsch,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:23.340 --> 00:00:30.300
Danny DeVito, Christopher Lloyd, Tony Danza,&nbsp;
Marilu Henner, and Andy Kaufman. In hindsight,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:30.300 --> 00:00:35.280
the show seemed too big to fail, and in&nbsp;
reality, it actually was too big to fail.

00:00:35.280 --> 00:00:41.340
"Taxi" ran for four seasons until 1982,&nbsp;
racking up Emmy wins and nominations and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:41.340 --> 00:00:46.980
becoming one of ABC's biggest commercial&nbsp;
successes. It seems ludicrous that ABC&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:46.980 --> 00:00:51.000
would ever cancel the program, which&nbsp;
was a sentiment echoed at the time,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:51.000 --> 00:00:54.000
with creator James L. Brooks&nbsp;
telling The Washington Post,

00:00:54.000 --> 00:00:58.200
"The one thing that's clear from this is&nbsp;
that the network is saying to everybody,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:58.200 --> 00:01:01.980
'Don't think Emmys will do you any&nbsp;
good when it comes to scheduling.'"

00:01:02.580 --> 00:01:08.700
After HBO declined to pick up the series, NBC came&nbsp;
to the rescue, restoring "Taxi" to its original&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:08.700 --> 00:01:14.340
time slot of Thursday nights following their hit&nbsp;
sitcom "Cheers." Sadly, the ratings failed to live&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:14.340 --> 00:01:20.160
up to NBC's expectations, resulting in its second&nbsp;
cancellation after only one additional season in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:20.160 --> 00:01:26.220
1983. However, most of the cast got to briefly&nbsp;
reunite to film re-enactments of "Taxi" scenes&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:26.220 --> 00:01:32.160
with Jim Carrey when the comedian starred in the&nbsp;
1999 biopic "Man on the Moon" as Andy Kaufman.

00:01:32.160 --> 00:01:37.920
Most television audiences became aware of&nbsp;
"Cagney &amp; Lacey" as a police procedural that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:37.920 --> 00:01:43.740
aired from 1982 to 1988 on CBS starring&nbsp;
Sharon Gless and Tyne Daly as detectives&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:43.740 --> 00:01:48.720
juggling their complex personal lives with&nbsp;
crime-solving in New York City. However,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:48.720 --> 00:01:53.940
most people only know its resurrected&nbsp;
state. It originally debuted as a pilot&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:53.940 --> 00:01:58.260
in 1981 starring Loretta Swit in&nbsp;
the role of Cagney alongside Daly,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:58.260 --> 00:02:03.720
while Meg Foster took over the role when it was&nbsp;
ordered to a six-episode first season in 1982.

00:02:03.720 --> 00:02:07.620
Following the show's first season,&nbsp;
CBS pulled it from their lineup,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:07.620 --> 00:02:13.020
citing poor ratings and audiences not connecting&nbsp;
with the two characters' aggression. This&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:13.020 --> 00:02:17.880
decision by the network resulted in backlash from&nbsp;
audiences, while the show's executive producer,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:17.880 --> 00:02:23.340
Barney Rosenzweig, tried to re-negotiate to get&nbsp;
the show put back on the air. Their compromise was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:23.340 --> 00:02:28.320
to recast Foster with Sharon Gless, who was&nbsp;
previously the first choice to play Cagney.

00:02:28.320 --> 00:02:32.640
The second season premiered to a rocky start,&nbsp;
with the show getting canceled for a second&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:32.640 --> 00:02:37.080
time in 1983, but fan outcry eventually&nbsp;
got it picked up for a third season,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:37.080 --> 00:02:43.080
which saw it receive a boost in the ratings. Gless&nbsp;
and Daly proved to be a dynamic onscreen duo,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:43.080 --> 00:02:49.380
resulting in the show lasting another four seasons&nbsp;
before CBS canceled it for good in 1988 after a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:49.380 --> 00:02:55.440
ratings decline, leaving its Season 7 cliffhanger&nbsp;
unresolved. Although a rebooted pilot in 2018&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:55.440 --> 00:03:00.420
couldn't get off the ground at CBS, the show&nbsp;
did see four TV movies since its cancellation.

00:03:00.420 --> 00:03:05.262
"What? That's bogus, man. This is public&nbsp;
property, you can't tell us where to surf."

00:03:05.262 --> 00:03:09.135
"Wrong, pal! You endangered lives.&nbsp;
It's my call. You're outta here."

00:03:09.135 --> 00:03:12.540
It's hard to believe that a show like&nbsp;
"Baywatch," which continues to hold the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:12.540 --> 00:03:17.820
record for the largest TV audience of all time,&nbsp;
ever struggled to grab the attention of audiences.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:18.600 --> 00:03:24.480
Premiering on NBC in 1989, the show starred&nbsp;
an ensemble cast featuring David Hasselhoff&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:24.480 --> 00:03:29.760
and Pamela Anderson, who would go on to become&nbsp;
some of the biggest celebrities of the 1990s.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:29.760 --> 00:03:35.520
However, after its first season aired, NBC quickly&nbsp;
put it to bed due to poor ratings and reviews.

00:03:35.520 --> 00:03:42.180
However, its reruns in countries like Germany and&nbsp;
the U.K. saved the show, as broadcasting company&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:42.180 --> 00:03:48.360
LBS Communications revived "Baywatch" in 1991.&nbsp;
"Baywatch" continued to air in its original form&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:48.360 --> 00:03:54.240
for 10 additional seasons throughout the '90s.&nbsp;
After its ninth season in 1999, the show was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:54.240 --> 00:04:00.720
restructured, recast, relocated to Hawaii, and&nbsp;
rebranded as "Baywatch: Hawaii" to save costs.

00:04:00.720 --> 00:04:06.600
As one would expect, the massive overhaul&nbsp;
of "Baywatch: Hawaii" didn't sit well with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:06.600 --> 00:04:10.680
audiences at the time, with the show facing a&nbsp;
steep decline in ratings until it was canceled&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:10.680 --> 00:04:17.160
in 2001 after 11 seasons. However, the "Baywatch"&nbsp;
brand has lived on through spin-off series,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:17.160 --> 00:04:23.460
a 2003 film, as well as a 2017 film&nbsp;
starring Dwayne Johnson, Zac Efron,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:23.460 --> 00:04:27.840
and Alexandra Daddario that was&nbsp;
panned by reviewers for many of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:27.840 --> 00:04:31.980
the same reasons the original "Baywatch"&nbsp;
series never garnered critical acclaim.

00:04:31.980 --> 00:04:36.480
"The truth is out there, but so are lies."

00:04:36.480 --> 00:04:39.840
"The X-Files" was a game-changer&nbsp;
for science-fiction television,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:39.840 --> 00:04:44.220
becoming one of the first shows of the 1990s to&nbsp;
gain a cult fanbase through the early internet.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:44.220 --> 00:04:50.280
Starring David Duchovny and Gillian Anderson as&nbsp;
FBI agents investigating paranormal occurrences,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:50.280 --> 00:04:55.740
"The X-Files" premiered on Fox in 1993 and&nbsp;
quickly rose to become the cult phenomenon&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:55.740 --> 00:05:00.660
that it currently is. However, the show didn't&nbsp;
maintain its well-deserved praise forever.

00:05:00.660 --> 00:05:07.320
The ninth season of "The X-Files," which aired&nbsp;
between 2001 and 2002, was victim to a drop in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:07.320 --> 00:05:12.420
ratings and poor reviews from television critics,&nbsp;
who cited the series' lackluster writing compared&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:12.420 --> 00:05:17.940
to its earlier, more inspired seasons. Fox&nbsp;
pulled the plug on the series, though its creator&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:17.940 --> 00:05:22.320
Chris Carter blamed the series' cancelation on&nbsp;
audiences' unwillingness to watch a show about&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:22.320 --> 00:05:27.900
conspiracies and corruption in the wake of the&nbsp;
September 11 terrorist attacks, telling Gizmodo,

00:05:27.900 --> 00:05:31.740
"There was lots more we could have&nbsp;
done but we ended at the right time."

00:05:31.740 --> 00:05:37.440
To the delight of many hardcore fans, Fox&nbsp;
gave "The X-Files" a second chance in 2016,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:37.440 --> 00:05:42.120
reviving it for a 10th season with&nbsp;
Duchovny and Anderson returning. The&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:42.120 --> 00:05:46.080
two actors also returned for an 11th&nbsp;
season, but following its conclusion,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:46.080 --> 00:05:51.480
Anderson officially parted ways with the show.&nbsp;
This brought the series to a premature end for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:51.480 --> 00:05:56.520
a second time as the creators currently have no&nbsp;
intention to continue on without Dana Scully.

00:05:56.520 --> 00:06:02.820
"7th Heaven" was a late hit of the 1990s,&nbsp;
premiering in 1996. The series, which centers&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:02.820 --> 00:06:07.920
on a Protestant family living in California with&nbsp;
seven kids of varying ages, quickly became a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:07.920 --> 00:06:14.160
hit on The WB network. However, the series was&nbsp;
subject to network shake-ups in 2006 after The&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:14.160 --> 00:06:19.140
WB was shut down during a merger with the United&nbsp;
Paramount Network to form a new channel: The CW.

00:06:19.140 --> 00:06:26.040
During the change, The WB canceled "7th Heaven"&nbsp;
after 10 seasons, mostly due to the series' high&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:26.040 --> 00:06:30.720
production costs and dwindling ratings compared&nbsp;
to The WB's other series like "Gilmore Girls"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:30.720 --> 00:06:36.180
and "Smallville." Additionally, some of the&nbsp;
show's biggest stars, such as Jessica Biel and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:36.180 --> 00:06:41.400
Barry Watson, had left the show in its later&nbsp;
seasons and were unlikely to return. However,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:41.400 --> 00:06:46.620
once the ratings spiked following the announcement&nbsp;
of the show's ending, The CW made the surprising&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:46.620 --> 00:06:50.700
decision to pick "7th Heaven" back up for&nbsp;
an 11th season to seize on the opportunity.

00:06:51.300 --> 00:06:55.860
Sadly, this decision didn't last long&nbsp;
at The CW. The series was once again&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:55.860 --> 00:07:00.300
canceled by the network in 2007 after&nbsp;
the end of the season. Even the show's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:00.300 --> 00:07:03.900
cast members have shot down recent&nbsp;
queries about a possible revival as&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:03.900 --> 00:07:08.220
recently as 2023 due to controversies&nbsp;
amongst some of the other cast members.

00:07:08.760 --> 00:07:12.660
Matt Groening is best known as the&nbsp;
co-creator of "The Simpsons," the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:12.660 --> 00:07:17.340
simultaneous longest-running animated series&nbsp;
and American sitcom on television. However,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:17.340 --> 00:07:20.940
he also garnered a cult fanbase&nbsp;
for his second animated series,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:20.940 --> 00:07:27.180
"Futurama," which premiered in 1999 on Fox.&nbsp;
"Futurama" centers on Philip J. Fry, a pizza&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:27.180 --> 00:07:32.460
delivery man who is mistakenly cryogenically&nbsp;
frozen and reawakens 1,000 years later, where&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:32.460 --> 00:07:37.260
he's hired by an intergalactic delivery company&nbsp;
alongside an eccentric ensemble of characters.

00:07:37.260 --> 00:07:42.660
Compared to "The Simpsons," the life span of&nbsp;
"Futurama" on Fox was short-lived due to its&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:42.660 --> 00:07:45.900
inconsistent airtime, resulting&nbsp;
in its cancellation in 2002.

00:07:45.900 --> 00:07:51.240
"Yes, I'm afraid the brainless drones who&nbsp;
run the network canceled our license."

00:07:51.240 --> 00:07:56.340
It wasn't until years later, after the show&nbsp;
had gained a second life through syndicated&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:56.340 --> 00:08:01.080
reruns and four direct-to-video movies, that&nbsp;
"Futurama" was picked up for its fifth season&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:01.080 --> 00:08:06.240
by Comedy Central, who continued to air it for&nbsp;
an additional two seasons after that. However,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:06.240 --> 00:08:10.980
the show was never on solid ground on&nbsp;
Comedy Central, producing several possible&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:10.980 --> 00:08:15.900
series finales until 2013, when its actual&nbsp;
finale, "Meanwhile," aired on the network.

00:08:16.500 --> 00:08:22.020
Until recently, "Futurama" was thought to be&nbsp;
long dead, but the impossible happened in 2022&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:22.020 --> 00:08:26.760
when Hulu ordered a revival of the series&nbsp;
to air on their streaming service. However,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:26.760 --> 00:08:31.980
this revival news came with controversy after&nbsp;
voice actor John DiMaggio threatened to not&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:31.980 --> 00:08:38.040
reprise his role as Bender without a pay raise for&nbsp;
the entire cast. Fortunately, once a new deal was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:38.040 --> 00:08:41.160
worked out, DiMaggio did end up returning.&nbsp;
Hopefully this time, it doesn't go away.

00:08:41.160 --> 00:08:44.520
"Family Guy" was the brainchild&nbsp;
of voice actor Seth MacFarlane,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:44.520 --> 00:08:49.140
centering on the Rhode Island-based Griffin&nbsp;
family and their various antics. Its first&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:49.140 --> 00:08:54.660
season was subject to good ratings in 1999, but&nbsp;
when its second season saw a decline in 2000,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:54.660 --> 00:08:59.280
Fox abruptly canceled the show, only to revive&nbsp;
it for a third season a few months later.

00:08:59.280 --> 00:09:03.180
Once "Family Guy" struggled to maintain&nbsp;
high ratings for its third season,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:03.180 --> 00:09:07.860
Fox canceled it yet again in 2002 and sold&nbsp;
the rights to Cartoon Network, who began&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:07.860 --> 00:09:13.140
airing reruns of the program on their late-night&nbsp;
Adult Swim programming block. It slowly gained&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:13.140 --> 00:09:17.280
more attention from Adult Swim's audiences,&nbsp;
and thanks to the additional sales of DVDs,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:17.280 --> 00:09:21.720
"Family Guy" was revived by Fox for&nbsp;
a second time in 2004. Thankfully,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:21.720 --> 00:09:26.580
MacFarlane kept an optimistic outlook about the&nbsp;
show's ups and downs, telling the Calgary Sun,

00:09:26.580 --> 00:09:29.280
"We really wanted to keep&nbsp;
the show exactly as it was."

00:09:29.280 --> 00:09:34.080
Since its fourth season return in 2005,&nbsp;
"Family Guy" has remained a staple of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:34.080 --> 00:09:40.260
Fox network and a consistent success. As of 2023,&nbsp;
"Family Guy" has aired a total of 21 seasons,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:40.260 --> 00:09:42.960
and MacFarlane has remained a&nbsp;
part of the show's voice cast.

00:09:43.560 --> 00:09:49.800
Debuting on ABC in 2001, "Scrubs" starred Zach&nbsp;
Braff as J.D., the daydreaming medical intern&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:49.800 --> 00:09:53.940
at Sacred Heart Hospital, who pines&nbsp;
for his fellow intern Elliot Reid,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:53.940 --> 00:09:58.740
played by Sarah Chalke. The show's early&nbsp;
seasons were beloved by critics and fans alike,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:58.740 --> 00:10:01.680
with Entertainment Weekly saying of it in 2006,

00:10:01.680 --> 00:10:05.880
"A likable, daffy, buoyant series&nbsp;
that would be a big annoying mess&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:05.880 --> 00:10:09.900
if it weren't done just right, Scrubs&nbsp;
is the very definition of nimble."

00:10:09.900 --> 00:10:14.700
However, "Scrubs" hit a brick wall when the&nbsp;
Writers' Guild of America went on strike from&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:14.700 --> 00:10:20.520
2007 to 2008, short-changing its seventh&nbsp;
season by seven episodes and ultimately&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:20.520 --> 00:10:25.200
dooming it to cancellation due to production&nbsp;
being stalled. After a period of not knowing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:25.200 --> 00:10:30.000
if "Scrubs" would continue airing, ABC picked&nbsp;
the show up for its eighth season. While this&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:30.000 --> 00:10:34.080
would be seen as a victory by some, it&nbsp;
would soon become bittersweet when it was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:34.080 --> 00:10:38.100
announced that Braff intended to depart from&nbsp;
the show's main cast at the end of the season.

00:10:38.100 --> 00:10:43.320
"Sometimes when you get what you want,&nbsp;
you end up missing what you left behind."

00:10:43.320 --> 00:10:48.600
"Scrubs" returned for its ninth season in 2009,&nbsp;
featuring a predominantly new cast of medical&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:48.600 --> 00:10:53.460
students at Winston University. Though Braff&nbsp;
appeared in six of the season's 13 episodes,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:53.460 --> 00:10:58.200
fans were adamantly opposed to the vast&nbsp;
changes in the show's formula. Eventually,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:58.200 --> 00:11:03.120
ABC announced that "Scrubs" was canceled in&nbsp;
2010, with Braff telling his Facebook followers,

00:11:03.120 --> 00:11:07.080
"It was worth a try, but alas... it didn't work."

00:11:07.680 --> 00:11:11.940
Thankfully, the world of Internet meme culture&nbsp;
has kept "Arrested Development" alive longer&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:11.940 --> 00:11:17.760
than any network could. Created by Mitch Hurwitz,&nbsp;
"Arrested Development" premiered on Fox in 2003,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:17.760 --> 00:11:22.500
led by Jason Bateman's Michael Bluth, the&nbsp;
son of a corrupt real estate developer who&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:22.500 --> 00:11:27.360
struggles to keep his family of narcissistic,&nbsp;
delusional, and financially struggling socialites&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:27.360 --> 00:11:32.580
together. The show boasted one of the strongest&nbsp;
ensembles in TV history, including David Cross,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:32.580 --> 00:11:38.160
Will Arnett, and Jessica Walter, as well as&nbsp;
up-and-comers Alia Shawkat and Michael Cera.

00:11:38.160 --> 00:11:43.620
After three seasons of low ratings on Fox,&nbsp;
"Arrested Development" was canceled by the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:43.620 --> 00:11:47.040
network, but Hurwitz was determined&nbsp;
to find a second home for the series.

00:11:47.040 --> 00:11:50.940
"I don't think the Home Builder's&nbsp;
Organization is going to be supporting us."

00:11:50.940 --> 00:11:53.520
"Yeah, the HBO is not gonna&nbsp;
want us. What do we do now?"

00:11:53.520 --> 00:11:55.320
"Well, I think it's Showtime."

00:11:55.320 --> 00:11:59.820
After years of failed starts and rumors of&nbsp;
a film, "Arrested Development" was finally&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:59.820 --> 00:12:06.540
revived by Netflix, which aired a fourth season in&nbsp;
2013 featuring the entire returning cast. However,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:06.540 --> 00:12:10.980
due to the conflicting schedules of the show's&nbsp;
cast, the season was structured to make each&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:10.980 --> 00:12:15.360
episode focused on an individual character, with&nbsp;
plotlines intersecting throughout the episodes.

00:12:15.360 --> 00:12:21.240
"Arrested Development" remained dormant for many&nbsp;
more years after the divisive fourth season. It&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:21.240 --> 00:12:26.400
wasn't until 2018 that the show finally returned&nbsp;
for the first half of its fifth season, with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:26.400 --> 00:12:31.980
a second half released in 2019. By this point,&nbsp;
tensions off-screen became tiresome for the cast,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:31.980 --> 00:12:37.260
including an incident of Jeffrey Tambor's&nbsp;
abusive on-set behavior. That, mixed with the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:37.260 --> 00:12:42.720
unfortunate passing of Walter in 2021, means that&nbsp;
"Arrested Development" is probably gone for good.

00:12:42.720 --> 00:12:44.764
"The show's gonna last three weeks!"

00:12:44.764 --> 00:12:46.200
"Six seasons and a movie!"

00:12:46.200 --> 00:12:49.980
Although "Community" captured a dedicated&nbsp;
fanbase from its very first episode,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:49.980 --> 00:12:55.980
behind the scenes the show struggled to stay&nbsp;
on the air. The NBC sitcom premiered in 2009,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:55.980 --> 00:13:00.000
starring Joel McHale as an ex-lawyer&nbsp;
forced to attend community college,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:00.000 --> 00:13:06.360
where he befriends a study group of misfits and&nbsp;
outcasts in an ensemble including Gillian Jacobs,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:06.360 --> 00:13:11.760
Alison Brie, Donald Glover, and Chevy&nbsp;
Chase. The show was created by future&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:11.760 --> 00:13:16.740
"Rick &amp; Morty" co-creator Dan Harmon, who was the&nbsp;
main catalyst for the show's off-screen troubles.

00:13:17.280 --> 00:13:22.800
After a public feud with Chase over disagreements&nbsp;
with the show's direction, Harmon was fired from&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:22.800 --> 00:13:28.740
season four of "Community," only to be rehired&nbsp;
after Chase himself left the show. Harmon returned&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:28.740 --> 00:13:33.360
for season five of "Community," but by that point&nbsp;
it was too little too late, and "Community" found&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:33.360 --> 00:13:39.480
itself on NBC's chopping block in 2014. However,&nbsp;
after adopting the tagline "Six seasons and a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:39.480 --> 00:13:43.740
movie" from a previous episode, fans were&nbsp;
determined to find the sitcom a new home.

00:13:43.740 --> 00:13:48.900
"Community" found its saving grace in Yahoo!&nbsp;
Screen, which ordered a sixth season of the show,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:48.900 --> 00:13:53.460
though by this point both Glover and Yvette&nbsp;
Nicole Brown had departed from the cast,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:53.460 --> 00:13:58.620
with others eyeing their post-"Community" futures.&nbsp;
Although some involved insisted that "Community"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:58.620 --> 00:14:04.920
was not canceled, Yahoo! Screen shut down in&nbsp;
2016, canning the series' future. To the delight&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:04.920 --> 00:14:10.080
of all "Community" fans, the long-awaited movie&nbsp;
was finally confirmed in 2022 to be happening.

00:14:10.080 --> 00:14:15.300
"Cougar Town" marked a triumphant return to&nbsp;
the sitcom format for Courteney Cox, who rose&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:15.300 --> 00:14:22.380
to fame by playing Monica on NBC's "Friends" from&nbsp;
1994 to 2004. On "Cougar Town," Cox plays Jules,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:22.380 --> 00:14:27.300
a recent divorcée re-exploring dating in her&nbsp;
40s, with an ensemble of her friends played&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:27.300 --> 00:14:32.820
by Dan Byrd, Busy Philipps, and Christa&nbsp;
Miller. The show premiered on ABC in 2009,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:32.820 --> 00:14:37.440
though faced many setbacks in its run,&nbsp;
including producers requesting a name change.

00:14:37.440 --> 00:14:43.380
Its biggest setback, however, came after the third&nbsp;
season, when ABC removed it from their mid-season&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:43.380 --> 00:14:48.780
schedule, priming the producers for a potential&nbsp;
cancellation. These predictions came to fruition,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:48.780 --> 00:14:53.940
but "Cougar Town" was thankfully saved by TBS,&nbsp;
who picked it up for a fourth season in 2013,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:53.940 --> 00:14:57.540
and then subsequently renewed&nbsp;
it for a fifth and sixth season.

00:14:57.540 --> 00:15:02.520
"I honestly thought we might never be&nbsp;
in this kitchen again. Just hanging out,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:02.520 --> 00:15:06.060
telling our stories to each other. To the world."

00:15:06.060 --> 00:15:12.420
Sadly for fans of the single-camera sitcom, TBS&nbsp;
opted to end its renewals after the sixth season,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:12.420 --> 00:15:17.340
rendering that the final season of "Cougar&nbsp;
Town" after it finished airing in 2015.

00:15:17.340 --> 00:15:20.760
Though the show was more prepared&nbsp;
than most for its series finale,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:20.760 --> 00:15:23.700
that doesn't mean the cast wasn't&nbsp;
disappointed that the show wouldn't&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:23.700 --> 00:15:28.860
continue on TBS. As Josh Hopkins, who&nbsp;
played Grayson in the show, told Variety,

00:15:28.860 --> 00:15:31.740
"I'm going to miss seeing those people every day,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:31.740 --> 00:15:35.820
but I just think what a great experience&nbsp;
it was, rather than be sad that it's over."

00:15:35.820 --> 00:15:42.300
"Nashville" premiered on ABC in 2012, centering&nbsp;
on Hayden Panettiere as a rising country star&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:42.300 --> 00:15:46.740
named Juliette Barnes who threatens the&nbsp;
power of Connie Britton's Rayna James.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:46.740 --> 00:15:51.300
The biggest draw to "Nashville," naturally,&nbsp;
was its music. The show included original&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:51.300 --> 00:15:55.680
songs and covers that were distributed by&nbsp;
Big Machine Records, the same Nashville&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:55.680 --> 00:16:00.420
label that formerly supported Taylor Swift's&nbsp;
rise to country stardom in the early 2000s.

00:16:00.420 --> 00:16:05.400
Sadly, "Nashville" was abruptly canceled by&nbsp;
ABC after its fourth season. The announcement&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:05.400 --> 00:16:09.600
came shortly after ABC confirmed that the&nbsp;
show would be heralded by new showrunners,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:09.600 --> 00:16:13.920
which meant that it would be renewed for a&nbsp;
fifth season. However, the renewal didn't&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:13.920 --> 00:16:18.780
come very quickly, so the show's fans resorted&nbsp;
to an online campaign to bring the show back to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:18.780 --> 00:16:23.400
life after many were disappointed at where&nbsp;
the fourth season left the series off. The&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:23.400 --> 00:16:28.200
show was revived on the CMT network in 2016,&nbsp;
a more than appropriate home for the show.

00:16:28.200 --> 00:16:33.780
Season five of "Nashville" premiered in 2016,&nbsp;
but fans were even more shocked by the series'&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:33.780 --> 00:16:37.740
turn of events, which saw Connie Britton's&nbsp;
character killed off in the first half of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:37.740 --> 00:16:42.000
the season. Though the show was renewed for&nbsp;
a final sixth season which aired in 2018,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:42.000 --> 00:16:45.720
CMT opted to not keep it going beyond that point.

00:16:45.720 --> 00:16:50.520
The future seemed hopeful for "Designated&nbsp;
Survivor" when it began. Starring Kiefer&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:50.520 --> 00:16:53.820
Sutherland as a man designated as&nbsp;
next-in-line for the U.S. presidency&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:53.820 --> 00:16:57.240
after a terrorist attack kills everybody&nbsp;
ahead of him in the line of succession,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:57.240 --> 00:17:01.680
the show premiered in 2016 on ABC with&nbsp;
lots of network support behind it.

00:17:01.680 --> 00:17:04.680
Rather than have a pilot ordered&nbsp;
like most shows typically do,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:04.680 --> 00:17:07.440
"Designated Survivor" was&nbsp;
ordered straight to series,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:07.440 --> 00:17:11.400
and was renewed for a second season within&nbsp;
a week of its first season finale airing.

00:17:11.400 --> 00:17:16.080
However, in a business decision almost&nbsp;
as jarring as the show's initial order,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:16.080 --> 00:17:22.800
ABC abruptly canceled "Designated Survivor" in&nbsp;
2018 after a high turnover of showrunners and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:22.800 --> 00:17:26.580
difficult production scheduling failed&nbsp;
to meet the network's expectations.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:27.240 --> 00:17:31.380
However, Netflix opted to renew the&nbsp;
show for a third season themselves,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:31.380 --> 00:17:36.540
as they had already handled the distribution of&nbsp;
"Designated Survivor" to international markets.

00:17:36.540 --> 00:17:40.440
Following its third season, Netflix&nbsp;
ultimately made the decision to not&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:40.440 --> 00:17:44.220
renew "Designated Survivor" any further,&nbsp;
with the company thanking Sutherland and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:44.220 --> 00:17:48.120
the crew for creating a satisfying&nbsp;
final season. Designated Survivor"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:48.120 --> 00:17:51.780
wasn't lucky enough to be revived beyond&nbsp;
the second chance that Netflix gave it.

00:17:51.780 --> 00:17:53.940
"Well, I really screwed that up, didn't I?"

00:17:53.940 --> 00:17:58.560
However, most fans of the series are&nbsp;
more than satisfied with how it ended.

00:17:58.560 --> 00:18:03.480
As far as network science fiction television shows&nbsp;
go, "Timeless" had quite an interesting premise,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:03.480 --> 00:18:08.400
focusing on a trio traveling through time to stop&nbsp;
a terrorist organization from altering historical&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:08.400 --> 00:18:13.140
events. "Timeless" was eventually canceled by&nbsp;
the network after the end of its first season.

00:18:13.140 --> 00:18:18.720
"Timeless" sadly suffered from poor ratings&nbsp;
during its run on NBC. Fans clamored for the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:18.720 --> 00:18:22.440
show to be revived by another network, but&nbsp;
to the surprise of the series' creators,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:22.440 --> 00:18:25.980
"Timeless" was renewed three&nbsp;
days later by NBC themselves,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:25.980 --> 00:18:32.220
albeit with a downsized episode order at only 10&nbsp;
episodes. However, this revival didn't last long,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:32.220 --> 00:18:36.780
as NBC canceled the show yet again in&nbsp;
2018 after the second season ended.

00:18:36.780 --> 00:18:40.260
This time around, "Timeless" fans&nbsp;
didn't have to wait too long to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:40.260 --> 00:18:43.800
see the series properly conclude.&nbsp;
In their second change of mind,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:43.800 --> 00:18:49.200
NBC ordered a two-part finale to wrap up the&nbsp;
series, airing as a Christmas special in 2018&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:49.200 --> 00:18:54.660
and featuring the time-traveling trio rewinding&nbsp;
to the Hungnam evacuation during the Korean War,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:54.660 --> 00:18:59.340
which occurred during Christmas 1950.&nbsp;
Thankfully, this two-part finale was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:59.340 --> 00:19:03.900
more than enough for fans to say goodbye to the&nbsp;
series that ran longer than NBC wanted it to.

